Delhi Power Consumption Analysis (2023)
An end-to-end data engineering and analytics project examining 24-hour power consumption patterns in Delhi — built with a full pipeline spanning NoSQL staging, ETL, SQL analytics, statistical testing, and BI dashboarding.

🎯 Problem Statement
Power utilities need to understand when and why demand spikes occur in order to manage grid load efficiently. This project analyzes hourly consumption data to answer:
When does peak electricity demand occur during the day?
Does consumption differ significantly between weekdays and weekends?
How does temperature influence load demand?
What actionable recommendations can utility providers draw from this?

🗂️ Dataset
Records: 8,737 hourly observations (one full year)
Fields: timestamp, temperature, load demand, solar generation, holiday indicator, weekend indicator, day of week, hour of day
Quality: No missing values or duplicates found during validation

